roup> <article-title>Polygyny and HIV in Malawi. <italic>Demogr Res</italic> 2009 (in press).</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="b24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>National Statistical Office (Malawi) and ORC Macro</collab> <source>Malawi Demographic and Health Survey 2000</source> <publisher-loc>Zomba, Malawi and Calverton, Maryland, USA</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>National Statistical Office and ORC Macro</publisher-name>, <year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="b25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stoneburner</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Low-Beer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Sexual partner reductions explain human immunodeficiency virus declines in Uganda: comparative analyses of HIV and behavioural data in Uganda, Kenya, Malawi, and Zambia.</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>33</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>20</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Partner reduction and the prevention of HIV/AIDS.</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>328</volume>:<fpage>848</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15073053</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> The Malawi Diffusion and Ideational Change Project has been funded by the National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (NICHD), grants R01-HD37276, R01-HD044228-01, R01-HD050142, R01-HD/MH-41713-0. The MDICP has also been funded by the Rockfeller Foundation, grant RF-99009#199.</p></fn><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing interests:</bold> None.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>